  "note": "One entry per thing the two Grade 6 tables say a learner must be able to do, across the four content areas (Numbers, Geometry, Measure, Graphs). `any` = covered when some question's stem or answer contains ANY of these phrases. `all` = covered only when ONE question contains ALL of them. Terms are matched against the question STEM AND ANSWER ONLY, never the explanation. ⚠ MATHS IS THE HARDEST PACK TO LEDGER, because a bare computation carries no words at all: '4 862 x 7 = ?' tests multiplication and contains neither 'multiply' nor 'multiplication'. Every term below was therefore chosen against the wording the corpus ACTUALLY uses, measured before the ledger was written — so a reported gap here means the topic is absent, not merely worded differently. ⚠ SHORT TERMS ARE TRAPS: 'mm' matches co-mm-on and 'cl' matches cl-assroom, so units are written out ('millimetre') or spaced (' mm '). ⚠ The Grade 6 tables are cumulative in spirit but not in text: what Grade 5 taught is not repeated here, so this ledger does not check Grade 5 work such as the four operations on whole numbers.",
